2020 was a crazy year during it we had a  global pandemic literally the entire  world ground to a halt governments  around the world went ahead and shut  down their economies they mandated  people sit inside and try to prevent the  spread of the virus well when all of a  sudden you slow down the velocity of  money you grind these economies to a  halt you say that there is no ability to  go to work or to go and participate in a  normal way you have to do something  because investors get scared those  investors got real scared in march of  2020 when they got scared all of a  sudden they started to sell every asset  it's called a liquidity crisis during a  liquidity crisis an investor looks at  their entire portfolio and they say what  do i own that i can sell today so that i  can get dollars the dollar is safe the  dollar is strong i want to hold dollars  in times of uncertainty and so those  investors started to sell every single  asset they had in their portfolio that  had a liquid market they held stocks  they sold them they held gold they sold  them if they had bitcoin they sold them  anything they could sell to get dollars  they were doing it equities went down  about 25  gold was down about 15  bitcoin dropped 50 percent in a single  day whenever you have a massive sell-off  in the market and then you have that  overlaid with the uncertainty of running  a business and having to actually get  rid of employees and costs or whether  they're labor or their actual production  cost now you have fear setting it you  have this ability where businesses and  their employees do not know the future  at that moment in march of 2020 the  federal government and also the treasury  and the federal reserve all came  together they had a bunch of discussions  and they finally decided they were going  to take action in a variety of ways this  began the great manipulation of the  monetary and fiscal policy what we saw  were two emergency rate cuts where we  brought interest rates down to a zero  rate environment in the u.s we also saw  the printing of trillions of dollars and  it was stuffed in every corner of the  financial system at the same time some  of that money some of those trillions of  dollars went to unemployment boost but  some of it also went to very exotic  elements of the financial system where  there was repo markets and all sorts of  other things that were occurring whether  it was through monetary or fiscal policy  they wanted to intervene they wanted to  step in they wanted to help but at the  same time they also said we have to give  direct support to people and so they  sent out stimulus checks those stimulus  checks ended up being hundred dollars in  the max in april of twenty twenty so you  could earn up to twelve hundred dollars  depending on your income in prior years  those twelve hundred dollars if you held  it today would be worth much less  inflation has been over five percent now  for a number of months that means the  rate of the price growth of various  goods in the economy has absolutely  exploded  but if you got that 1200 check as  stimulus and you put it into bitcoin a  finite asset an asset that cannot be  debased by anyone it is not controlled  by anyone and you held it till today it  would now be worth over 10 000 u.s  dollars that's right those stimulus  checks that 1200 check if you had taken  it you'd converted it from a fiat  currency that was going to be devalued  at historic pace and you converted it  into an asset that no one could debase  as a global store of value that 1200 is  now worth over 10 000  absolutely incredible to see once people  start to learn how do i actually store  value wealthy people have been doing  this for literally centuries they take  their currencies and they convert them  into hard assets whether it's real  estate or some other type of commodity  there's all sorts of strategies that  people employ a lot of it is  underwritten by what is their risk  profile what is their liquidity needs  and what is the ability to actually make  money what is the price appreciation  look like as well but now what we see is  we have this digital decentralized  currency that digital decentralized  currency has become a global store of  value it is accessible to billions of  people around the world and what people  were able to do is they were able to  take that 1200 check they were able to  convert it from that fiat depreciating  asset into an asset that cannot be  debased that asset is now trading at a  much much higher rate than it was  previously and so when you get that  price appreciation you not only get the  preservation of purchasing power but you  also get the appreciation of purchasing  power which is exactly what bitcoin has  done at high rates of inflation what we  saw investors do is they literally  dropped gold gold is down seven percent  on a nominal basis it's down double  digits on a real return basis and they  instead chose bitcoin as the inflation  hedge we saw paul tudor jones and q3 of  last year say if i am going to believe  that there's going to be high rates of  inflation i want to own inflation hedge  assets but i think that bitcoin is going  to be the fastest horse and so he  allocated a single digit percentage of  his portfolio to bitcoin ends up that  paul tudor jones was right he was  quickly followed with public  announcements from everyone from stanley  druckenmiller to a bunch of other  well-respected institutions and  individual investors but the beauty of  bitcoin is that it is available to  anyone literally individuals around the  world front ran all of these hedge funds  and wall street institutions for years  beforehand all you needed was an  internet connection you could go on to  the web and you could go ahead and you  could purchase bitcoin you could convert  some of your other assets into an asset  that cannot be debased by anyone so that  1200 check that went out in april 2020  is now worth over ten thousand dollars  you can sit around and you can complain  about what is going on from monetary or  fiscal policy  or you can learn exactly what wealthy  people do you can learn how they protect  their purchasing power how they  appreciate their portfolio and how they  continue to put themselves in a better  and better financial position over time  that's what bitcoiners have done and  that's what you can do twelve hundred  dollars april 2020 now with over ten  thousand dollars that's the beauty of an  asset that can't be debased by anyone  else
 

